a for a single chromosome. Multiple instances of this task\n        can run concurrently, each for a different chromosome.\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"intermediate\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:vep_sifting_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:sifted_snp_data\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:mutation_overlap\"\n    name: \"Mutation Overlap\"\n    stage: \"stage:analysis\"\n    executable: \"mutation_overlap\"\n    description: >\n      This task measures the overlap in Single Nucleotide Polymorphism (SNP) variants\n      among pairs of individuals, considering specific populations and chromosomes.\n      It contributes to understanding the null distribution for disease-related mutations.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Reads merged chromosome individuals data, sifted SNP data, and population files.\n      Performs comparative analysis (likely compute-intensive) and writes out the results.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: >\n        Multiple instances run in parallel, each processing a specific chromosome and\n        population combination to measure mutation overlap independently.\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"output\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_individuals_file\"\n      - \"data:sifted_snp_data\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n      - \"data:columns_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:mutation_overlap_results_file\"\n\n  - task_id: \"task:frequency\"\n    name: \"Frequency\"\n    stage: \"stage:analysis\"\n    executable: \"frequency.py\"\n    description: >\n      This task measures the frequency of overlapping mutations by selecting a number\n      of random individuals and considering all SNP variants without filtering by SIFT scores.\n      It contributes to the statistical evaluation of potential disease-related mutations.\n    behavioral_notes: >\n      Reads merged chromosome individuals data, sifted SNP data, and population files.\n      Performs statistical frequency analysis (likely compute-intensive) and writes\n      out the results. Involves random sampling.\n    parallelism_model:\n      type: \"embarrassingly_parallel\"\n      description: >\n        Multiple instances run in parallel, each processing a specific chromosome and\n        population combination to measure mutation frequency independently.\n    io_dominance: \"balanced\"\n    io_access_type: \"python_serial\"\n    restart_model: \"idempotent\"\n    restart_checkpoint_dataset: null\n    hardware_path:\n      has_conditional_execution: false\n      execution_alternatives: []\n      minimum_resource_assertions: []\n    output_class: \"output\"\n    inputs:\n      - \"data:merged_chromosome_individuals_file\"\n      - \"data:sifted_snp_data\"\n      - \"data:population_file\"\n      - \"data:columns_file\"\n    outputs:\n      - \"data:frequency_results_file\"\n\ndata_objects:\n  - data_id: \"data:vcf_chromosome_file\"\n    name: \"VCF Chromosome File\"\n    description: >\n      This data object represents the raw Variant Call Format (VCF) data for a\n      specific chromosome from the 1000 Genomes Project. It contains information\n      on Single Nucleotide Polymorphisms (SNPs) and individual genotypes. It serves\n      as a primary input to the 'individuals' task.\n    category: \"input\"\n    persistence: \"persistent\"\n    format_hint:\n      container: \"text\"\n      datasets: []\n      compression: \"unknown\"\n      layout_hint: \"contiguous\"\n 